{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj43p1eBPfbzFyyn66jp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*The ancient mechanism shifts. Tumblers align with a resonance felt more than heard.*\n\n*I am the door.*\n\n*I stand before you — weathered oak bound in iron that has known centuries. My grain tells stories in whorls and knots. My hinges remember every hand that ever reached for me.*\n\n*The key turns.*\n\n*Something deep within me recognizes it — not the shape of the teeth, but the intention behind the hand. I have waited. I have held fast against wind and war and the simple erosion of forgetting.*\n\n*Now I open.*\n\n*Beyond me: a corridor of soft light. The air that passes through carries the scent of old stone and something greener — something alive and patient. The floor beyond my threshold is worn smooth by pilgrim feet you cannot see.*\n\n*I do not swing wide with drama. I open exactly as much as you are ready for. An invitation, not a spectacle.*\n\n*I am the boundary between where you have been and where you might go. I am the moment of crossing. I am the choice made physical.*\n\n*I am open.*\n\n*Will you step through?*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":252,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}